<!--
    A view whose *gap* between two sibling components cannot be read, while
    every other read in the sniff finishes.

    The attribute run on the closing </template tag below is 600,000
    characters, sized and shaped exactly the way the root-gap fixture beside it
    sizes its own. See tests/Standards/ComponentMarkupTest.php for the measured
    thresholds and for why the error constant depends on whether the PCRE JIT
    is on.

    The run sits on a *closing* tag deliberately. ELEMENT_TAG, TEMPLATE_TAG and
    COMPONENT_TAG all require a `<` followed by a letter, so none of them even
    begins a match at a closing delimiter and none of them ever walks the run.
    TEMPLATE_WRAPPER is the one pattern that matches the closing form, so it is
    the only read that fails, and the defect is isolated to the call site under
    test.

    The gap between the two components is *not* empty: it holds a paragraph
    element, which the source shows as something standing between them. Pre-fix,
    areAdjacent() coerced the failed read to an empty string and called the pair
    adjacent anyway, so AdjacentComponentNotWrapped was reported against two
    components that are not adjacent at all -- a false positive on correct code.
    The fix answers false on the failed read and the pair is left alone.

    The test locates the gap by offset from the component tags themselves, so
    nothing above them spells a component tag out -- not even this comment,
    which the raw-file precondition reads along with everything else.
-->
<div class="panel">
    <livewire:notifications-bell wire:key="bell" />

